  "multi_gpu_followup": {
    "source": "tools/v41/engine/ds41_mgpu.{cpp,hpp} in the same read-only Xolotl working tree",
    "source_cpp_sha256": "e5ae88b7bf0436d35e53a2aef37df0731845ac68cb45f45a73d78828c8d88896",
    "source_hpp_sha256": "240e5444b9230bc98635b5b4f8565b383ba14489624efaa066facac687ded466",
    "destination": "tools/v41/engine/ds41_runner.{cpp,hpp}",
    "adjustments": "Adapt the layer-sharded production runner separately from the earlier all-resident prototype. Add strict selection parsing, global pinned-tail budgeting, aligned cache sizing, preflight/coverage checks, device-input staging and default auto CUDA-device selection. Reject unsupported pruning/speculation explicitly; retain CPU and explicit single-GPU paths."
  },
  "port_adjustments": [
    "All fork headers, CPU pool/native/PTQ kernels, CUDA IQ/MMVQ fork helpers and elastic cache remain private; do not link their same-named but different-ABI symbols with upstream Strata engine libraries.",
    "Compile unchanged upstream CPU IQ and platform helpers again with private headers; finite-clamp IQ gate/up uses stock ggml dot products instead of requiring modified upstream IQ kernel APIs.",
    "Build stock ggml CUDA in a separate project sharing the exact selected ggml sources, link only its backend archive and initialize it directly; no global ggml target or registry patches.",
    "Keep PDL graph launches disabled, fused DS41 patches absent, MMQ unsupported with explicit CLI error, DSpark optional OFF, and uncommitted multi-GPU wrapper/flags excluded coherently.",
    "Fix optional-DSpark-off compilation and reject disabled speculative environment switches before loading a model.",
    "Add self-contained standard GGUF and full-width mixed-pool fixtures; extend CUDA reference parity to standard Q2_K with finite SwiGLU clamp."
  ],
